// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6322 Add detection rule for insecure SMBv1 enablement
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6322
// Pull request author: fabjan4u
// Change: new rule
// Title: Insecure SMBv1 Protocol Enablement
// Sigma ID: d421ceee-0a4c-4ecd-8e11-0f0478618433
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Fabian Cras (mboRijnland / CIV Smart Technology)
// Date: 2026-09-23 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense-evasion, lateral-movement, T1562.001, T1021.002
// Description: Detects attempts to re-enable the deprecated and insecure SMBv1 protocol via PowerShell cmdlets,
//   DISM, or Service Control Manager. Adversaries may enable SMBv1 to exploit legacy vulnerabilities
//   (e.g. EternalBlue) or conduct lateral movement.
// False positives:
//   - Rare administrative deployment of legacy application dependencies
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/storage/file-server/troubleshoot/detect-enable-and-disable-smbv1-v2-v3
//   - https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/alerts/2017/01/16/risks-using-smbv1
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/a3ae7b8b8d0d2a1aa1ee9e67e69105d770fab7dd/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_insecure_smbv1_enablement.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "Set-SmbServerConfiguration" and ProcessCommandLine contains "-EnableSMB1Protocol" and ProcessCommandLine contains "$true") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "Enable-WindowsOptionalFeature" and ProcessCommandLine contains "SMB1Protocol") or (FolderPath endswith "\\dism.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/enable-feature" and ProcessCommandLine contains "SMB1Protocol")) or (FolderPath endswith "\\sc.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "config" and ProcessCommandLine contains "mrxsmb10" and ProcessCommandLine contains "start="))
